---
import { MCP_POINTS } from "../data";
---

<section
  id="mcp"
  class="border-y border-pz-line bg-pz-sand px-6 py-20 lg:py-28"
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl">
    <div class="grid gap-14 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_0.85fr] lg:gap-20">
      <div>
        <p
          class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-pz-clay-strong"
        >
          In your own AI
        </p>
        <h2
          class="mt-4 font-heading text-3xl font-semibold leading-tight md:text-4xl"
        >
          Give the assistant you already use a permanent briefing on your family.
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-pz-ink-soft">
          Most people who'd get value from Parenza already have an AI assistant
          open all day. Rather than asking you to move, Parenza plugs into it.
          Ask Claude or ChatGPT a question about your child and it can consult
          your family's actual record — and the same specialist panel — before it
          answers.
        </p>

        <dl class="mt-10 space-y-7">
          {
            MCP_POINTS.map((point) => (
              <div class="border-t border-pz-line-strong pt-5">
                <dt class="font-heading text-lg font-semibold text-pz-ink">
                  {point.title}
                </dt>
                <dd class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed text-pz-ink-soft">
                  {point.body}
                </dd>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </dl>

        <p class="mt-8 text-sm leading-relaxed text-pz-ink-mute">
          The mechanism is MCP — an open standard for connecting an AI assistant
          to a source of data. You don't need to know that to use it: you copy an
          address, and your assistant handles the rest. What it means for your
          data is spelled out on the{" "}
          <a
            href="/trust"
            class="text-pz-clay-strong underline underline-offset-2"
            >Trust &amp; Security</a
          >{" "}page.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="lg:pt-16">
        <div
          class="overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-pz-line bg-pz-paper shadow-[0_24px_60px_-32px_rgba(43,37,33,0.4)]"
        >
          <div class="border-b border-pz-line bg-pz-cream px-5 py-3">
            <span
              class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-pz-ink-soft"
              >Connect Parenza</span
            >
          </div>
          <div class="space-y-5 px-5 py-6">
            <div>
              <p class="text-xs text-pz-ink-mute">Endpoint</p>
              <p
                class="mt-1.5 rounded-lg border border-pz-line bg-pz-cream px-3 py-2.5 font-mono text-xs text-pz-ink"
              >
                https://mcp.parenza.ai
              </p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <p class="text-xs text-pz-ink-mute">Works with</p>
              <div class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
                {
                  ["Claude", "ChatGPT", "Claude Code", "Cursor"].map((c) => (
                    <span class="rounded-full border border-pz-line-strong px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-pz-ink-soft">
                      {c}
                    </span>
                  ))
                }
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="border-t border-pz-line pt-5">
              <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-pz-ink-soft">
                You sign in once in your browser to authorize the connection.
                Nothing is shared with an assistant you haven't connected.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-3 text-center text-xs text-pz-ink-mute">
          Connection panel as it appears in the app. Endpoint shown is the
          production address for design partners.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-pz-line bg-pz-cream p-6">
          <p
            class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-pz-ink-soft"
          >
            What you can then ask, anywhere
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-pz-ink-soft">
            {
              [
                "How much did she actually take over the last 24 hours?",
                "We're travelling next week — what changes about the routine?",
                "What did we decide about the vitamin D dose, and why?",
                "Summarize the last two weeks for the six-week check.",
              ].map((q) => (
                <li class="flex gap-3">
                  <span
                    class="mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-pz-sage"
                    aria-hidden="true"
                  />
                  <span>&ldquo;{q}&rdquo;</span>
                </li>
              ))
            }
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
